ons":["us-east-2","us-east-1","us-west-1"],"service_name":"AWS Secrets Manager"},{"change":-0.3144444449999999,"current_cost":0.735,"percent_change":-21.83641979166666,"regions":["us-east-2","us-east-1","us-west-1"],"service_name":"Amazon Virtual Private Cloud"}]},"last_updated":"2026-01-16T05:59:02.122404","metadata":{"analyzed_services_count":8,"granularity":"DAILY","is_complete":true,"period_days":31,"regions_count":10,"total_amortized_cost":5464.615456046215},"report":"# Financial Cloud Cost Optimization Report\n\n**Prepared for:** Executive Leadership\n**Date:** October 26, 2023\n\n---\n\n## 1. Financial Health Score\n\n| Score | Rationale |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **35 / 100** | **Poor.** This score reflects critically low visibility into current expenditure and operational efficiency. The failure of automated analysis prevents identification and remediation of waste, translating directly to unmanaged financial risk. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Executive Summary\n\nThis report analyzes the core operational cloud spend, totaling **\\$5,305.31** for the analyzed period (assuming Unblended and Amortized costs are equivalent due to lack of allocation data).\n\nThe analysis was critically hampered by API rate limits, resulting in a complete failure of the automated cost intelligence engine to perform deep utilization analysis, rightsizing recommendations, or savings calculation.\n\n*   **Total Spend Analyzed:** **\\$5,305.31** \ud83d\udcb0\n*   **Top Spend Driver:** Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (EC2 Compute) at **\\$2,687.02** (50.6% of total spend). \ud83d\udcc8\n*   **Total Potential Savings Identified:** **Undetermined.**\n*   **Immediate Action Required:** Repair the data ingestion pipeline to restore financial oversight and accountability.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Critical Financial Risks\n\nThe primary financial risk facing Cloud Operations is the **lack of transparency and control.**\n\n*   \u26a0\ufe0f **Data Integrity Failure:** The automated analysis failed across all services due to API rate limits. This means the organization is operating blind, with high confidence of significant unmanaged waste (idle resources, oversized instances, forgotten volumes).\n*   \u26a0\ufe0f **Compute Cost Concentration:** 70% of the total budget is concentrated in compute (EC2 and OpenSearch). Without utilization metrics, we cannot confirm if this spend is driving necessary business value or merely funding oversized infrastructure.\n*   \u26a0\ufe0f **Exposure to Spot Volatility (Potential):** Without optimization data, we are unable to enforce reservation strategies (RIs/Savings Plans) or manage high-cost on-demand usage, exposing the business to unnecessary spend volatility.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Prioritized Savings Pipeline\n\nThe pipeline below focuses on mandatory manual deep dives, prioritized by the dollar volume of the service, as these represent the areas of highest potential ROI. Estimated savings remain unquantified (Unquantified, High Probability) pending data restoration.\n\n| Service Area | Optimization Category | Description | Estimated Savings (Annualized) | Difficulty | Priority |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| EC2 - Compute | Rightsizing & Lifecycle | Manual review of 19,291 usage hours for termination, rightsizing, and commitment modeling. | Unquantified (High) | Medium | 1 (Immediate) |\n| Amazon OpenSearch | Rightsizing & Index Mgmt. | Manual deep dive into cluster utilization and index retention policies. | Unquantified (High) | Medium | 2 (High) |\n| EC2 - Other | Cleanup & Allocation | Manual review of orphaned EBS volumes, snapshots, and data transfer costs. | Unquantified (Medium) | Medium | 3 (Standard) |\n| EKS | Cluster Efficiency | Manual review of EKS cluster utilization and scaling strategies. | Unquantified (Medium) | Medium | 4 (Standard) |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Key Recommendations\n\nWe must immediately shift focus from strategic optimization to fundamental data governance and cost hygiene.\n\n### \ud83d\ude80 **Action 1: Fix Cloud Intelligence Data Pipeline**\n\nThe highest ROI action is fixing the source of this analytical failure. Work with DevOps and Cloud Governance teams to identify and remediate the API rate limits causing data ingestion failures. Until the automated system can provide utilization data, all optimization efforts are high-effort, low-scale manual tasks.\n*   **Metric:** Time to full data ingestion recovery.\n\n### \ud83d\ude80 **Action 2: Initiate Compute Fleet Utilization Scrub**\n\nImmediately deploy engineering resources to perform a manual review of the EC2 and OpenSearch fleets (50.6% and 20.0% of total spend, respectively). This review must focus on identifying 24/7 non-production workloads, zero-utilization instances, and prime candidates for Rightsizing or Reserved Instance commitments.\n*   **Deliverable:** A list of 5 instances totaling >\\$500 in monthly spend targeted for termination or rightsizing within the next 10 days.\n\n### \ud83d\ude80 **Action 3: Establish Financial Visibility SLA**\n\nInstitute a Service Level Agreement (SLA) for financial data reporting. The Cloud Operations team must ensure that cost intelligence tools operate with 99.9% uptime for data ingestion to maintain financial control. Failure to comply with this SLA must trigger immediate remediation and executive notification.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Data Integrity Note\n\nThis Financial Cloud Cost Optimization Report is based on **incomplete data**. Detailed utilization metrics, specific resource identifiers, and historical spending patterns necessary for calculating precise savings projections were unavailable due to widespread API rate limits encountered during the automated deep analysis phase. All identified savings potential is currently *unquantified*. The figures provided reflect only the gross reported spend for the services listed.","total_account_cost":5464.615456046215}
